[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own reports say
otherwise. Read by tenant instead of by subject or intake tag, they split into two problems
with two different fixes. Each has its own ticket. Five reports the desk read as a one-day move
are counted under their cause and tracked on their own.

<Callout>
#4471 closed on 5 October. <b>parser</b>: fixed (<code>fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales</code>).
<b>hint</b>: won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired. The tickets below are closed to match.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2', 'one-day move': 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/3' }} />

- **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Day and month swap.
- **hint**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as
  told, and the form reads the date day first. This happens only through the form, and only for
  booking-v3 tenants.
- **one-day move** (within parser): the date moves by one day, not by a swap. It looks like a
  timezone problem. The desk had already read these reports this way (desk notes) and counts them
  under parser. The parser fix doesn't name them, so watch for new one-day reports.

## How this was counted

- One id, one report: the ticket export repeats some reports across pages.
- Cause by tenant (locale and booking form), with `causeOf` in `causes.ts`. The intake tag is a
  guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant often enough that it can't be
  used for counting.
- Counted the desk's way: one-day moves stay under their tenant's cause, as the desk files them,
  and are shown on a row of their own. The desk's own table:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes on the desk

- Do not merge a date report into #4471 on its subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Check the tenant and the channel first, with the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe).

